So Thick Mint is a new Ben & Jerry's Topped flavour in the US. We can't get it over here in the UK and we can't get the Mints themselves either!

If you like mint...... GO FOR IT as the mint balls are AMAZING. 
If you don't like mint, avoid like a minty plague. 

What you'll need to make all this is.....

The Ice Cream Base:
350ml Milk at 1.8%
300ml Cream @ 49%
90g Sugar
40g Dextrose
30g Golden syrup/ Corn Syrup
35g Skimmed Milk Powder
2tsp Mint extract (good quality)

The Cookies (adjusted recipe):
150g Butter , softened
200g Sugar
1 Egg
1 tsp vanilla extract
200g flour
50g Dutched cocoa powder
1 tsp  baking soda
Combine and bake at 175c for 10-12 minutes. 

The Ganache Top:
50g of 50% Dark Chocolate
1tbps water
Combine and melt in the microwave checking every 10 seconds. 

There are lots of parts to making this ice cream and if you use the 50% chocolate as mentioned in the video, the top will be more successful. You can always use Coconut oil, vegetable oil or cream to make a normal ganache if you wish. 

